{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"wsmcp","version":"devel"},"instructions":"WsMcp emulates the WonderSwan, the WonderSwan Color and the SwanCrystal. No machine runs until a cartridge is in: cart_load {path} puts one in, and emu_status says what runs. A frame is 1/75.47 s; video_screenshot shows the LCD. Addresses are linear, 0 to $FFFFF, or \"SSSS:OOOO\" strings; integers may be written as hex strings, \"0x1000\" or \"$1000\". The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"audio_capture_start","description":"Keeps the machine's sound from now on, every run's, until audio.capture_stop writes it: stereo at 24 kHz, the four channels and Hyper Voice mixed as the headphones hear them (or the speaker, as the emulator is set), 16 bits.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"audio_capture_stop","description":"Ends the capture, and writes what it kept to path as a WAV: 16-bit stereo at 24 kHz.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the WAV."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"cart_info","description":"The cartridge the machine runs: its path, the model running it, what its header says (publisher, game id and version, colour support, whether it is held vertically, the checksum and whether the ROM sums to it, the 16 bytes whole), its ROM's size and CRC-32, the sizes of its SRAM, its EEPROM and the console's EEPROM, and whether the boot ROM ran, with its CRC-32.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"cart_load","description":"Puts a cartridge in and powers the machine up with it, running the boot ROM when the BIOS directory has the model's. The saves of the cartridge that ran are written back first, and the new one's read from the save directory. Without model, a cartridge whose header supports colour, or a .wsc file, runs on a WonderSwan Color, any other on a WonderSwan. On failure what ran runs on. Answers as cart.info.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The ROM file, .ws or .wsc."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"ws (WonderSwan), wsc (WonderSwan Color) or sc (SwanCrystal); chosen by the cartridge when left out."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"cart_save","description":"Writes the cartridge's SRAM or EEPROM, and the console's EEPROM, to the save directory now, as a power-up and the emulator's end do. Nothing is written without a save directory.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"cpu_disassemble","description":"Disassembles instructions as the V30MZ would fetch them, without the side effects of reading, in Mesen2's syntax (MOV AX, DS:[BX+SI+$04]); a relative jump shows the offset it lands at. Given as \"SSSS:OOOO\", the walk keeps to that segment, IP wrapping in it; given linear, it is taken in the current CS when CS reaches it, else as offset (address & $FFFF) of segment (address >> 16) * $1000.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"Where to start: linear, 0 to $FFFFF, or \"CS:IP\" such as \"F000:FFF0\"."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, 1 to 1000."}},"required":["address","count"]}},{"name":"cpu_get_state","description":"The V30MZ's registers at the instruction boundary the machine stands at: CS:IP and its linear address pc, the general registers AX BX CX DX SP BP SI DI, the segments DS ES SS, the flags as a number and as ODITSZAPC (a capital for a set flag), whether HLT halted it until an interrupt, the instruction at CS:IP, and the cycle it begins in.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_add","description":"Stops runs before the instruction at an address. The instruction the machine stands at runs when it runs on.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The instruction's linear address, 0 to $FFFFF, or its \"CS:IP\" such as \"F000:FFF0\"; a breakpoint is by linear address, whatever segment reaches it."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_list","description":"The breakpoints' linear addresses, ascending.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_remove","description":"Removes the breakpoint at an address. Answers whether there was one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The instruction's linear address, or its \"CS:IP\"."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_trace","description":"The history of execution, counted back from now: index 0 is the newest instruction, the one the machine stands at, 1 the one that ran before it, and so on, over the last seconds debug.trace.configure sets (0.5 by default). Answers count of them from index from, newest first, each with the cycle it began in, CS:IP and its linear pc, the registers before it, and its bytes and disassembly as they were when it ran.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many, 0 to 4096; 32 when left out."},"from":{"type":"integer","description":"The newest one's index, 0 being the newest kept; 0 when left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_trace_configure","description":"How many seconds of the machine's time the history of execution keeps, 0.01 to 10, from now and after every power-up. A second is at most 3,072,000 instructions, some 50 bytes each.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"seconds":{"type":"number","description":"The history's length."}},"required":["seconds"]}},{"name":"debug_trace_find","description":"Searches the history of execution back from index from, 0 being the newest, for instructions that meet every condition given, and answers up to limit of them, newest first, as debug.trace does. next_from continues the search where it stopped, or is null when it reached the oldest.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pc":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The instruction's linear address, or its \"CS:IP\"."},"pc_start":{"type":"integer","description":"With pc_end: the instruction's linear address is at least this."},"pc_end":{"type":"integer","description":"With pc_start: the instruction's linear address is below this, up to $100000."},"disasm_contains":{"type":"string","description":"Its disassembly, as it ran, holds this text, case aside: OUT, CALL, [$0400]."},"ax":{"type":"integer","description":"AX before it."},"bx":{"type":"integer","description":"BX before it."},"cx":{"type":"integer","description":"CX before it."},"dx":{"type":"integer","description":"DX before it."},"sp":{"type":"integer","description":"SP before it."},"bp":{"type":"integer","description":"BP before it."},"si":{"type":"integer","description":"SI before it."},"di":{"type":"integer","description":"DI before it."},"cs":{"type":"integer","description":"CS before it."},"ds":{"type":"integer","description":"DS before it."},"es":{"type":"integer","description":"ES before it."},"ss":{"type":"integer","description":"SS before it."},"from":{"type":"integer","description":"The index to search back from; 0, the newest, when left out."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"The most matches to answer, 1 to 4096; 32 when left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_add","description":"Stops runs after the instruction that reads or writes data in a range of memory, or of I/O ports with port: any access of its own beyond fetching its bytes, a DMA's included. One per address and space; a second replaces the first.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The range's first address: linear, 0 to $FFFFF, or \"SSSS:OOOO\"; with port, a port, 0 to $FFFF."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"Bytes or ports in the range; 1 when left out."},"access":{"type":"string","description":"read, write (the default) or access for both."},"port":{"type":"boolean","description":"Watch I/O ports rather than memory; false when left out."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_list","description":"The watchpoints: address, size, access, and whether they watch ports.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_remove","description":"Removes the watchpoint at an address. Answers whether there was one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The range's first address, or its first port with port."},"port":{"type":"boolean","description":"The watchpoint is on I/O ports; false when left out."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"emu_pause","description":"Pauses the machine where it runs by itself: in the desktop application, which then runs it only on request. wsmcp-cli runs only on request anyway.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_reset","description":"Switches the machine off and on: the WonderSwan has no reset button. The cartridge and the boot ROM are read again, the saves written back and read again, every part starts as at power-up and time from 0; breakpoints, watchpoints and the trace start empty. On failure the machine runs on.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_resume","description":"Lets the machine run by itself again, where it does: in the desktop application.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_run_cycles","description":"Runs cycles of the 3.072 MHz clock, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles to run at least."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_frames","description":"Runs through frame boundaries, where the PPU hands a finished picture over, 75.47 a second, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Frame boundaries to run through."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_until","description":"Runs until a condition holds, checked at every instruction boundary: the V30MZ about to run the instruction at pc; a byte of memory holding a value; or the bytes sent to the serial port and not yet read by serial.read holding a text. Give one or more; any of them stops it, and condition says which.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pc":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"Stop before the instruction at this address: linear, 0 to $FFFFF, or \"CS:IP\" such as \"F000:FFF0\"."},"memory_equals":{"type":"object","description":"{\"address\", \"value\"}: stop when the byte at the address, linear or \"SSSS:OOOO\", holds the value."},"serial_contains":{"type":"string","description":"Stop when the bytes sent to the serial port since the last serial.read hold this text."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles after which to give up; 61,440,000 (20 s) when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_set_bios_directory","description":"Reads the boot ROMs from a directory from now on, as bootrom.ws, bootrom.wsc and bootrom_sc.wsc or under No-Intro's names, and powers the machine up again with the cartridge it runs. On failure the directory and the machine stay as they were.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The directory."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"emu_status","description":"The emulator's version, whether the window's own run is paused, and, when a machine runs, which one (ws: WonderSwan, wsc: WonderSwan Color, sc: SwanCrystal), the cartridge it runs, whether it ran the boot ROM, and its time: cycles of its 3.072 MHz clock and frames (75.47 a second) since power-up, and where the last run stopped at a breakpoint or a watchpoint. When none runs, why.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_step","description":"Runs V30MZ instructions, one when count is left out, stopping before at a breakpoint or after a watched access. The cycles a halted CPU waits for an interrupt are not instructions: a step from HLT runs until the interrupt comes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, 1 to 1,000,000."}}}},{"name":"input_clear","description":"Lets go of every button the protocol holds.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_get","description":"The buttons the protocol holds, by the hardware's names (x1-x4, y1-y4, a, b, start, sound), and as a mask. The desktop application's keyboard and pads hold their own beside these.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_hold","description":"Holds exactly these buttons down, letting go of any other, until told otherwise. The machine does not run.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"buttons":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"The buttons' names, as input.press takes them; [] lets go of all."}},"required":["buttons"]}},{"name":"input_press","description":"Presses buttons together for some frames, lets them go, and runs some frames more, running the machine as it goes; buttons input.hold holds stay held. Names: x1-x4 (the X pad: x1 up, x2 right, x3 down, x4 left, also up, right, down, left), y1-y4 (the Y pad, likewise), a, b, start, sound. A vertical game is held turned and reads the pads turned with it: which button is its up is the game's to say. A breakpoint or watchpoint that stops the hold lets the buttons go, and answers so.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"buttons":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"The buttons' names: [\"a\"], [\"x1\", \"b\"]."},"frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames to hold them, 1 to 600; 6 when left out."},"release_frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames to run after letting them go, 0 to 600; 6 when left out."}},"required":["buttons"]}},{"name":"input_set","description":"Holds a button down, or lets it go, until told otherwise. The machine does not run.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"button":{"type":"string","description":"The button's name, as input.press takes it."},"down":{"type":"boolean","description":"Down, or up."}},"required":["button","down"]}},{"name":"io_get_state","description":"Every device's registers as the debugger keeps them: the PPU (mode, screens 1 and 2 with their scroll and map, the windows, sprites, LCD icons and shades; a latched register with the copy the line is drawn with), the APU's four channels and Hyper Voice, the timers, the DMAs, the interrupt controller (active and enabled IRQs, vector), the keypad, the serial port, the console's and the cartridge's EEPROMs, and the cartridge's bank registers ($C0-$C3).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"io_read","description":"Reads I/O ports as the V30MZ's IN would, but without a read's side effects: the serial port's data and status, $B1 and $B3, and the keypad's, $B5, read 0. The WonderSwan's ports are $00-$FF; the 16-bit I/O space above them mirrors them or answers nothing.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"port":{"type":"integer","description":"The first port, 0 to $FFFF."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many consecutive ports, 1 to 256; 1 when left out."}},"required":["port"]}},{"name":"io_write","description":"Writes an I/O port as the V30MZ's OUT would, with every effect the write has, but beside the bus: no cycle passes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"port":{"type":"integer","description":"The port, 0 to $FFFF."},"value":{"type":"integer","description":"The byte, 0 to $FF."}},"required":["port","value"]}},{"name":"memory_list_regions","description":"The memory regions memory.read and memory.write address, what each holds, whether it can be written, and its size in the machine running (null when none runs).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_read","description":"Reads bytes without the side effects a read by the V30MZ has. Without region, from the CPU's 20-bit address space as it is mapped now (work RAM at $00000, SRAM at $10000, ROM banks at $20000-$FFFFF, the boot ROM over the top while it is enabled); with region, from one of memory.list_regions' memories, by offset.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The first byte: without region a linear address, 0 to $FFFFF, or \"SSSS:OOOO\"; with region its offset."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"How many bytes, at most $100000."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"work_ram, rom, save_ram, boot_rom, internal_eeprom or cart_eeprom; the CPU's address space, cpu, when left out."}},"required":["address","size"]}},{"name":"memory_write","description":"Writes bytes as a debugger does: no bus cycle is made and no device runs. Without region, into the CPU's address space, where every byte must fall on RAM or SRAM mapped there; with region, into work_ram, save_ram, internal_eeprom or cart_eeprom by offset. The whole range is checked first, so it is written whole or not at all.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":["integer","string"],"description":"The first byte: without region a linear address, 0 to $FFFFF, or \"SSSS:OOOO\"; with region its offset."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, two hex digits each."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"work_ram, save_ram, internal_eeprom or cart_eeprom; the CPU's address space when left out."}},"required":["address","data_hex"]}},{"name":"serial_read","description":"The bytes the cartridge has sent out of the serial port (the EXT port's UART, 9600 or 38400 baud) since the last serial.read, or since power-up: as hex, and as text with every byte but printable ASCII, tab, line feed and carriage return shown as a dot. Nothing is connected to the port: what is sent is kept, and nothing is received.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"state_list","description":"The .wsstate files in the state directory, by name.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"state_load","description":"Restores a state state.save wrote, of the same model with the same cartridge, by this build. On failure the machine runs on as it was.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"The state's file."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"state_save","description":"Writes the whole machine's state to a file: all a run changes, the cartridge's SRAM or EEPROM and the console's EEPROM included, without the ROMs, breakpoints, watchpoints or the trace. A name without a directory is in the state directory; .wsstate is the extension state.list looks for.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write it."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"video_screenshot","description":"The last complete picture: the LCD's 224 by 144 dots (with the LCD's icons beside or below them when the emulator shows them), in its own grey shades on a WonderSwan and its colours on a Color. A vertical game draws on its side, as the LCD is held turned; vertical says so. Written to path as a PNG, or returned as one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the PNG; left out, it is returned."},"scale":{"type":"integer","description":"Each dot as scale by scale pixels, 1 to 8; 1 when left out."}}}}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"version\":\"devel\",\"paused\":false,\"running\":false,\"error\":\"no cartridge is in\"}"}],"isError":false}}
